        "IB Diploma papers are sat in May, with results in early July, and a smaller November session with results in January. Cambridge IGCSE runs a February-March series in India for some subjects, then May-June and October-November, and Pearson Edexcel adds a January window beside its summer and autumn ones. Your school or exam centre confirms exact dates.",
        "Western Odisha's summer is the first obstacle. Daytime temperatures in April and May regularly pass 40 degrees Celsius, so a mid-afternoon lesson in a closed flat is a poor plan. Early morning or after dusk works far better, and the monsoon that follows, with Sundargarh district averaging roughly 1,650 mm of rain a year, brings its own power interruptions.",
        "The festival year is full and varied. Raja and Rath Yatra fall in June and July, Nuakhai, the western Odisha harvest festival, and the Karma festival kept by the district's tribal communities come around August and September, Durga Puja and Diwali fill October and November, and Christmas is significant for the district's Christian families in December.",
        "A workable plan uses this rhythm rather than fighting it: heavy practice in the quieter weeks, light consolidation around festivals, and a mock exam finished before the Puja break. For Diploma students, Class 11 internal exams, IA deadlines in Class 12 and predicted grades in autumn all need space in the same calendar.",
