  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Rajagangapur?", answer: "No school in Rajagangapur has been confirmed for the IB or for Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE. Local options are CBSE, ICSE and the Odisha board, and the nearest confirmed IB and IGCSE campuses are in Bhubaneswar, about 400 km away. Most families here therefore study these syllabuses through an online school or private tuition." },
    { question: "Will an IB Gram tutor come to my house in Rajagangapur?", answer: "No. Home visits run only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. In Rajagangapur every lesson is live and online, one to one, with a shared whiteboard, so it is private tuition taken at home on a laptop rather than a tutor arriving at the door." },
    { question: "How does online tuition work for a student in the OCL township?", answer: "A laptop, a headset and a steady connection are enough. The tutor joins a video call at the agreed time, writes on a shared whiteboard and works through past papers with the student. A phone hotspot makes a sensible backup, and a missed slot is rescheduled within the week." },
    { question: "What if power or broadband fails during a lesson?", answer: "The tutor waits briefly, then the slot is moved to another time that week. Keep a charged phone for a hotspot and tell us which months bring the worst cuts, such as the pre-monsoon heat, so regular lessons can sit in steadier hours." },
    { question: "Which boards and programmes do you cover?", answer: "IB and IGCSE tutors in Rajagangapur cover IB PYP, MYP, Diploma and CP, plus Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel IGCSE. Tutors are matched to the exact subject, level and exam series, for example IB Chemistry HL for May or Edexcel Mathematics A Higher for January." },
    { question: "How much does IB or IGCSE tuition cost for a family here?", answer: "It depends on programme, level, subject, session length and the tutor's recent experience with the syllabus. IB Gram publishes no price list; the rate is sent in writing after the free trial and before you book. Nothing is added for travel, because every session is online." },
    { question: "Can my child take IGCSE papers as a private candidate?", answer: "Generally yes, through an approved exam centre, which must be booked early. Centres, dates and entry deadlines vary by city, so confirm them first. A tutor prepares your child for the papers; the centre, not IB Gram, handles registration and entry." },
    { question: "Should we move to Bhubaneswar for the IB Diploma?", answer: "Only if the family wants a full classroom programme, since Bhubaneswar, about 400 km away, has the nearest confirmed IB Diploma and IGCSE schools. Some families start with online tuition in Class 9 or 10 to test fit. A tutor can continue after a move, which keeps the syllabus continuous." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with the Internal Assessment or Extended Essay?", answer: "Tutors coach; they never write. They can help narrow a question, explain what each criterion rewards, sanity-check a method and give frank feedback on a draft. The assessed work itself, including every sentence of the essay or write-up, stays entirely the student's own." },
    { question: "Which language should my child study: Odia, Hindi or English?", answer: "English is the language of instruction for IB and IGCSE, and the second language depends on your target university. Sundargarh district is multilingual, with Odia, Sadri, Mundari and Hindi all spoken. Hindi is widely understood, so many students take it; confirm available options with the school or exam centre." },
    { question: "Does IB or IGCSE help with NIT Rourkela, JEE or NEET?", answer: "It can, but check eligibility first. IB and IGCSE-based records can be used for Indian entrance routes subject to equivalence and subject rules, which change by year. IB Gram tutors teach the IB and IGCSE subjects; for test preparation, see the admissions page linked below." },
    { question: "When should a Class 9 or Class 11 student begin?", answer: "As close to the start of the course as possible, since that leaves time to close gaps before internal exams and Internal Assessment deadlines. A late start in the final year is still useful if sessions aim narrowly at past papers and the topics carrying the most marks." },
    { question: "How do lessons fit around shift work, heat and festivals?", answer: "Slots are set around your household: evenings, weekends or early mornings. In April and May, lessons shift away from the afternoon heat, and Nuakhai, Karma, Durga Puja and Diwali are treated as real breaks. An extra slot before an exam series is easy to add." },
    { question: "What happens in the free trial lesson?", answer: "Your child works on a real topic from their own syllabus with the proposed tutor, live on video, at no cost. You then see a short plan and a written rate. There is no obligation, and you can ask for a different tutor if the fit does not feel right." },
    { question: "What if we are not happy with the tutor?", answer: "Say so and we arrange a replacement, with no penalty. Sessions are reviewed every few weeks anyway, and the written notes after each lesson make it easy to see whether progress matches the plan." },
    { question: "How do we start from Rajagangapur?", answer: "Email support@ibgram.com or message +91 7439 368 115 on WhatsApp with the programme or board, subject, level and preferred hours. We reply with matched tutor profiles and a time for the free trial." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram linked to any school or exam board?", answer: "No. IB Gram is independent of the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge, Pearson and every school named on this page. Tutors follow the syllabus and mark scheme each board has published, and your school's own calendar." },
  ],

